From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SR_team <me@sr.team>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 03:00:00 +0500
Subject: [PATCH] nvk: align the stencil copy plane to the binding granularity

The D32_SFLOAT_S8_UINT stencil copy plane has its own VA mapping, like
ordinary tiled image planes. Its offset must satisfy the kernel backend's
binding alignment as well as NIL's image alignment. ZCULL storage or small
image planes can otherwise leave it at an offset RM cannot map.

---
 src/nouveau/vulkan/nvk_image.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/nouveau/vulkan/nvk_image.c b/src/nouveau/vulkan/nvk_image.c
index f473e5b33a1..7c81cbc194c 100644
--- a/src/nouveau/vulkan/nvk_image.c
+++ b/src/nouveau/vulkan/nvk_image.c
@@ -1213,7 +1213,7 @@ nvk_image_init(struct nvk_device *dev,
                           "Invalid image creation parameters");

       image->stencil_copy_temp.plane_align_B =
-         image->stencil_copy_temp.nil.align_B;
+         MAX2(image->stencil_copy_temp.nil.align_B, pdev->nvkmd->bind_align_B);
    }

    uint64_t plane_offset_B = 0;
